---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | yamltojson.net"
  description="Read the Privacy Policy for yamltojson.net. We guarantee 100% browser-based data processing with zero server tracking or data storage."
  canonicalUrl="https://yamltojson.net/privacy/"
>
  <Header />

  <main class="flex-1 bg-canvas transition-colors duration-200">
    <!-- Hero Header -->
    <section class="py-12 sm:py-20 mesh-gradient-bg border-b border-hairline">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-mute bg-canvas-elevated border border-hairline px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-4 shadow-2xs">
          LEGAL & DATA PROTECTION
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink mb-4">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-body max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          At yamltojson.net, your privacy is our top priority. Learn how our 100% browser-based architecture protects your data.
        </p>
        <p class="text-xs text-mute font-mono mt-3">
          Last Updated: October 3, 2026
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Main Policy Content -->
    <section class="py-16">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="bg-canvas-elevated p-6 sm:p-10 rounded-xl border border-hairline shadow-2xs space-y-8 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
          
          <!-- Section 1 -->
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight">
              1. 100% Client-Side Processing Guarantee
            </h2>
            <p>
              Unlike conventional web utilities, <strong>yamltojson.net</strong> operates entirely on your local device. When you paste text into our converter or upload a file (`.yaml`, `.yml`, `.json`, `.txt`), all parsing, syntax validation, and formatting occur inside your web browser using client-side JavaScript Web Workers and Web APIs.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Your input data, file contents, code strings, and API keys are NEVER transmitted across the internet to any server owned by us or third parties.</strong>
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 2 -->
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight">
              2. Data We Do Not Collect
            </h2>
            <p>Because our application architecture is stateless and backend-free, we do not collect, store, or log any of the following:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
              <li>No user input text, YAML strings, or JSON outputs.</li>
              <li>No uploaded file contents or metadata.</li>
              <li>No personally identifiable information (PII) such as names, physical addresses, or passwords.</li>
              <li>No user account data or login credentials.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 3 -->
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight">
              3. Local Storage & Preferences
            </h2>
            <p>
              We may use standard browser <code>localStorage</code> strictly for non-sensitive user experience settings—such as saving your active conversion options or indent preferences. This data remains exclusively stored on your local browser instance and can be cleared at any time through your browser settings.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 4 -->
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight">
              4. Cookies & Analytics
            </h2>
            <p>
              We do not use tracking cookies or intrusive advertising profiles. We may utilize lightweight, privacy-focused web telemetry (such as standard server access logs or privacy-compliant analytics) to measure overall site traffic, page views, and performance metrics. These logs contain only anonymous data such as browser type, general geolocation region, and timestamp.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 5 -->
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight">
              5. Third-Party External Links
            </h2>
            <p>
              Our website may contain references or links to external open-source projects, developer documentation (such as Astro or Tailwind CSS), or specifications. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of third-party external websites.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 6 -->
          <div class="space-y-3 border-t border-hairline pt-6">
            <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight">
              6. Contact Us Regarding Privacy
            </h2>
            <p>
              If you have any questions or security inquiries regarding this Privacy Policy or our client-side architecture, please reach out via our <a href="/contact/" class="text-link hover:underline font-medium">Contact Us page</a> or email us directly at <code>privacy@yamltojson.net</code>.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
